@title EPISODE 09 • STUDY SESSION
@bg library_night
@show priya
Priya: Stats midterm is in thirty-one hours. You have a forty-eight. I'm not judging. I'm calculating.
London: You're definitely judging.
Priya: Both. I'm a multitasker. Also I invited Diggy. He has a ninety-four.
London: You did WHAT.
@show diggy
Diggy: Relax, Sterling. I don't bite. I just tutor.
> [Bitchy] "I'll fail on my own, thanks." -> s1
> [Good] Swallow your pride and open the textbook. -> s2
> [Sweet] "...Okay. Teach me. Slowly." -> s3
*s1
@add Diggy_Affection -1
@add Grades -1
You last eleven minutes alone before you text him "where is the formula for standard deviation."
Diggy: (reading it out loud from across the table) Oh, she DOES need me.
@jump s_done
*s2
@add Grades 2
@add Coach_Respect 1
Three hours. Two Red Bulls. One breakthrough. Priya pretends not to notice your hands touching over the calculator.
@jump s_done
*s3
@add Grades 2
@add Diggy_Affection 2
He explains it like a race. "Mean is your average split. Deviation is how far you be wildin' from it." It's stupid. It works.
*s_done
@hide
@bg campus_quad_night
@show diggy
He walks you to your car at 1 a.m. even though it's forty feet away.
Diggy: Can I say something without you getting mad?
London: No promises.
Diggy: You're smart. Like actually. You just act like it's embarrassing to try.
> [Sweet] "Nobody's ever said that to me." -> w1
> [Bitchy] "Did you rehearse that?" -> w2
> [Bold] "And you act like it's embarrassing to want things." -> w3
*w1
@add Diggy_Trust 2
@add London_Confidence 2
He holds your car door open. You sit there for a full minute before you can drive.
@jump w_done
*w2
@add Diggy_Affection 1
Diggy: (laughing) A little. In the elevator.
@jump w_done
*w3
@add Diggy_Trust 3
That stops him. He looks at you like you just read his diary out loud.
*w_done
@load s1/ep10.mvs
